glue -- combine two networks
****************************

Description
===========

This function takes two reaction networks, or a reaction network and a list and
creates a new, combined network.

+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : N1 = reactionNetwork("A <-- 2B, A + C <-- D, B + E --> A + C")|
|                                                                   |
|o1 = 2B-->A                                                        |
|     D-->A+C                                                       |
|     B+E-->A+C                                                     |
|                                                                   |
|o1 : ReactionNetwork                                               |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : glue(N1, {"A --> 2B", "A + C --> D", "D --> B+E"})            |
|                                                                   |
|o2 = A-->2B                                                        |
|     2B-->A                                                        |
|     A+C-->D                                                       |
|     D-->A+C                                                       |
|     D-->B+E                                                       |
|     B+E-->A+C                                                     |
|                                                                   |
|o2 : ReactionNetwork                                               |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+

