twoSiteModificationE -- an example for chemical reaction motif
**************************************************************

Description
===========

A two-site phosphorylation system in which modifications are carried out by
different kinases and phosphatases for each phosphoform. Simply, it is assumed
that both phosphorylation and dephosphorylation occur sequentially.

+---------------------------+
|i1 : twoSiteModificationE()|
|                           |
|o1 = S_0+E_1-->X_1         |
|     X_1-->S_0+E_1         |
|     X_1-->E_1+S_1         |
|     S_1+E_2-->X_2         |
|     X_2-->S_1+E_2         |
|     X_2-->E_2+S_2         |
|     S_1+F_1-->Y_1         |
|     Y_1-->S_1+F_1         |
|     Y_1-->S_0+F_1         |
|     S_2+F_2-->Y_2         |
|     Y_2-->S_2+F_2         |
|     Y_2-->S_1+F_2         |
|                           |
|o1 : ReactionNetwork       |
+---------------------------+

